  "slug": "basal-ganglia-29a7",
  "summary": "New brain atlases and tools span mouse metadata harmonization, human cortical QTLs, hypothalamus and cerebrovascular disease, supporting reuse of cell-type data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is cell-type-resolved brain molecular data used to interpret disease and aging, with infrastructure for reuse. Resource papers include harmonized metadata and processed transcriptomes for wild-type and Alzheimer's disease model mouse sc/snRNA-seq, a multi-omic QTL atlas from 231 human prefrontal cortex donors tying disorder risk to cell-type and developmental regulation, and scCVD, which integrates scRNA-seq and ATAC-seq across 701 samples and over 4.68 million cells. HypoAD pairs MRI from 458 people with 614,403 snRNA-seq nuclei to map hypothalamic volume and cell-type changes in ageing and Alzheimer's disease. VEGABrain projects bulk RNA-seq onto developing human brain atlas surfaces with precomputed ssGSEA maps. A tensor decomposition study integrates hippocampal and colonic multi-omics in mice. Species, tissues and modalities vary across these works.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
